lete theory on that  just yet you'll also notice that these  moblins and bokoblins are walking within  spreading malice on the ground heavily  implying that these monsters that we've  been battling in breath of the wild are  in fact made of malice which is also  proven by the blood moon cutscene next  we are shown a wider shot of mysterious  individual that opened the trailer  surrounded by what appears to be  floating symbols that we commonly  associate with the zonai and some  unknown writing on the bottom left the  deity seems to be positioned atop a  floating island which makes sense given  all the other floating islands we see in  the sky as the shot pans up we can see  that there are seven of these stones and  as zelda fans know by heart seven is the  number of sages that were responsible  for sealing ganon away now we have to  wonder how exactly this ancient  civilization and this particular deity  are possibly connected to the sages of  legend the next shot is especially  mysterious it shows a girl with pointed  ears seemingly being either sacrificed  or otherwise lifted upward into the sky  with what looks to be malice underneath  the same individual is then shown  cupping hands with somebody else someone  whose hand is larger with bracelets  adorning the wrist if you'll recall  we've seen this hand before this is the  exact hand of the new deity complete  with the larger fingers and the bracelet  who could also be none other than the  green hand shown off in the very first  trailer above them just out of sight is  potentially two more of these symbolic  stones positioned together in a way that  mimics the sun it's also noteworthy that  this girl shown cupping hands here is  the same girl that was shown previously  levitating upward with the same pointed  ears long flowing hair and dress this  can only be assumed to be zelda but the  problem is the zelda that we know of  does not have longer hair anymore so  this is either a prophecy about our  zelda or it's a previous one maybe even  the first one but more on that later  immediately following this shot is one  of our familiar hero link sporting the  new shield shown in the previous trailer  opening a giant stone door into this sky  world or skyrule as i like to call it  this door is adorned with symbology as  well there is most notably the giant  circular twin dragon-like symbol  positioned front and center that also  appears once again at the end of the  trailer as the logo for the game on the  circle is more mysterious writing that  was shown previously on the wall most  intriguingly though is the eye symbol  that link touches in order to open the  door this could be representative of his  eyes opening to the new world or it  could as most fans know be a form of the  shika eye symbol which further  strengthens the theory that this ancient  race and the chica are connected also  it's notable that not only are the twin  dragons shown to be in a circular  pattern but this also seems to mimic the  cupping hands shown between zelda and  the deity implying that they are twins  once link opens the doors we are greeted  with the knowledge that he is already on  a sky island he then sprints forward  giving us a better view of the empty  shrine located directly in front of him  the camera then abruptly cuts to a  backward angle of link's sprinting but  it's clearly a different setting than  what we were just shown since the giant  doors he just opened are not visible and  the ground now features much more plant  life the camera swoops around link  showing off some structures located  behind him that features some sort of  buildings on top as well as a giant  cliff and another floating mini island  which has trees and some other  structures present once the camera shows  what's in front of link we then see more  sky islands and a particular giant  structure directly ahead off in the  distance this structure has a layered  design pattern that seems to call back  to the design of the mysterious deity  shown at first perhaps it is the temple  where this individual is located we are  shown many other sky islands in the  distance but it's presently impossible  to tell what's exactly going on with  each one of them so we'll move on for  now lincoln dives headfirst off the  island he was on showcasing once again  the highlight of the upcoming title  which is ascension and descension  between two worlds as link dives through  the clouds you can then dimly see the  familiar landscape of hyrule underneath  we are then shown link jumping onto and  clinging to a slab of rock within the  faron jungle region that appears to have  fallen down from skyrim which he then  uses his new powers to reverse through  time and return to its original position  using this to ascend this slab of rock  also appears to be associated with these  mysterious stone fragments in the water  on hyrule's surface also giving heavy  implications to the ancient race being  zonai which are the people responsible  for the stone fragments scattered  throughout the area the next shot is  back to link but as lots of fans are  speculating potentially another link  from another time it's very peculiar  that they still show this link with long  hair and rudimentary gear as opposed to  this link with the extremely familiar  and more modern hylian gear this  long-haired link is shown to be climbing  sky islands but everything is dark  implying that either this is night or  that this is somehow under the ground  also he's climbing up a root of a tree  implying that it was once under the  ground meaning that these sky islands  may not have always been in the sky the  next and final shot of the trailer is  also one of the most telling we see blue  link diving down to hyrule but this is  clearly hyrule after ganondorf has  already raised the castle which is  spewing a new deadly form of malice  that's also shown to be spewing out of  death mountain perhaps malice is now  corrupting lava as well as water like it  did in the first game as link falls we  can see more small islands scattered  around as well as a giant one in the  distance and we can also see more of the  ancient rune drawings also present  underneath hyrule castle link then  proceeds to land on an upgraded much  bigger glider that he can actually kneel  and ride on top of instead of hanging on  to the underside and we know that he'll  still be using a new version of the  classic glider from the previous trailer  so this seems to be a much more hardy  glider that he'll use simply to glide  more quickly in order to cover much more  ground since he'll be able to glide  anywhere in hyrule after jumping down  from sky rule link then appears to be  heading towards a mountain and the name  is escaping me currently but it's a  familiar one that now also has this  ancient runic drawing on it i'm not sure  if this means that these are the only  spots link will be able to land or if it  implies some sort of event happening at  these marked locations but either way  link is clearly heading towards it  lastly as link glides towards the marked  mountain we can see the familiar circle  dragon logo form out of the green  ancient energy as the logo fades in and  we're blatantly shown who zelda was  cupping hands with right behind the  words it is none other than the deity  that we saw at the first now this is the  end of the trailer but i have a theory  that i'd like to present before wrapping  up that has some very very very strong  implications of being true as we can see  there are many similarities between the  new deity and who i'm presuming is zelda  they both have long ears triangular  markings under the eyes circular  paddings that look like jewelry adorning  their bodies and they're heavily implied  to be symbolic of the twin dragons that  equal one another it could be that due  to this deity sporting long ears and the  ancient people serving it that this is  none other than the goddess hylia  herself and her original hylian race or  perhaps the original chica race or  perhaps a combination of both called the  zonai this added to the fact that this  deity's green energy can be used to  repair the master sword makes me think  that it must mean that we are returning  to the original hylia before the events  of skyward sword and that she will be  able to repair her sword her goddess  blade with her green energy and perhaps  that green link is the original hero and  perhaps hailey's tears for her kingdom  will finally be explained and the reason  why nintendo considered it a spoiler is  because we will finally know why the  sheikah symbol is an eye with a tear but  that's just a theory one that needs to  be fleshed out more but i'm pretty sure  is  more or less accurate what did you guys  think of the trailer are you happy with  the new name tears of the kingdom let me  know in the comments below i am beyond  stoked for this game and will likely be  covering it more so be sure to leave a  like on this video to spread it around  and subscribe if you haven't already to  stick around for so much more follow me  on my socials and that's all i've got  for this one this is bandit signing out  peace  [Music]
 

